<font size="2" color="#FFFFFF">
"<img src="o.jpg" height=50 width=50 border=0 alt="O">ut of the nothingness that existed before time, a consciousness formed. It had no shape, consisting of
pure fluid energy floating in an abyss of emptiness. As this entity grew and learned it became self aware.
It knew loneliness. And it grieved. It searched the void for others like it, but only found nothingness.
The millennia passed. . .during this time the entity became stronger and deeper entrenched in its
loneliness. In anger and fear it took all of its energy and threw it into itself to create matter as we
know it today. Its consciousness was no longer, but the energy it had created possessed the miracle of
life. This particle of matter began to multiply and grew to form the shape of something entirely unknown
in the universe. Like the one who created it, this being was self aware, but it had form as well as
consciousness. The energy of its creator flowed deeply in its veins for deep in its
being it felt the loneliness of the one before it and dreaded the same fate . . . "<br><br>
</font>
